venus 0112: read only GPU probe for the Adreno 660 of the venus board

The GPU of the Mi 11 (SM8350, Adreno 660, KGSL class) has no driver: the iOS
UI runs on the CPU rasteriser.  This patch adds the first, honest milestone
of the GPU work - a probe that proves the silicon is there and says what it
is, without trying to drive it.

It maps the 256 KiB KGSL 3D AHB aperture (0x3d00000, "kgsl_3d0_reg_memory")
and the GPU_CC clock controller (0x3d90000, "qcom,lahaina-gpucc") read only,
reads the GPU identity bytes, the clock gates (gpu_cc_ahb_clk, gpu_cc_cx_gmu_clk,
the GMU root clock) and the power domain status (GX and CX GDSC), and prints
one compact summary line every 5 s.

It never writes to the GPU: not to the AHB aperture, not to a GDSC, not to
the GX soft reset and not to a clock gate.  It publishes no IOKit service, so
the iOS userland keeps using the CPU rasteriser (a fake accelerator would
move CoreAnimation onto the Metal path and freeze the UI, see
logs/research/07-gpu-plan.md section 4.3).

Boot args: sweetgpu=1 (default off), sweetgpuaddr=<hex> (override the AHB
window), sweetgpuprobe=1 (the periodic line).

